# {{project_name}}

An atomic swap contract that exchanges two token amounts between two parties
in a single authorized transaction, generated by
[soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge) from the
`atomic-swap` template.

## How it works

Both parties authorize the `swap` call. The contract transfers `amount_a` of
`token_a` from party A to party B, and `amount_b` of `token_b` from party B
to party A. If either transfer fails, the entire transaction reverts — neither
side loses funds.

## Develop

```sh
cargo test
stellar contract build
```

## Deploy to testnet

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

Then invoke:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <PARTY_A> \
  --network testnet \
  -- swap \
  --party_a <PARTY_A_ADDRESS> \
  --party_b <PARTY_B_ADDRESS> \
  --token_a <TOKEN_A_ADDRESS> \
  --token_b <TOKEN_B_ADDRESS> \
  --amount_a 100 \
  --amount_b 50
```

